      "writtenOn": "2023-08-31T18:55:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure we need to use the shlex for this as we\u0027re really just looking to print it to the console. I was initially going to suggest that we use `logging.info` or `logging.debug` for this but apparently we\u0027re not using `logging` in this module (yet?).  Maybe the simpler solution is to just break this into two lines, one to build the string and one to print it. \n\n```suggestion\ndef run(cmd: List[str]) -\u003e int:\n    \"\"\"Run a command locally with the command echoed first.\"\"\"\n    cmd_string \u003d \" \".join(cmd)\n    print(f\u0027\u003e {cmd_string}\u0027)\n```",
      "parentUuid": "84442a9c_64b51d5b",
      "revId": "e44f2ef4bcb2ef1603e586520aa822ee55b410db",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
